From: gts7l project
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: reject widths not divisible by 4 with the
 wide bus

With the wide bus (two pixels per clock) a 1366x768 mode gives a sheared,
tilted and flickering picture on SM8250; 1360x768 and 1280x720 on the
same monitors are fine. Filter such modes out in mode_valid so userspace
picks the next one.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index dc6f33809..55a63b380 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -709,6 +709,14 @@ enum drm_mode_status msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	msm_dp_display = container_of(dp, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 	link_info = &msm_dp_display->panel->link_info;
 
+	/*
+	 * With the wide bus (2 pixels per clock) a width that is not a
+	 * multiple of 4 gives a sheared, flickering picture (seen on SM8250
+	 * with 1366x768 monitors; 1360x768 and 1280x720 are fine).
+	 */
+	if (msm_dp_wide_bus_available(dp) && mode->hdisplay % 4)
+		return MODE_H_ILLEGAL;
+
 	if ((drm_mode_is_420_only(&dp->connector->display_info, mode) &&
 	     msm_dp_display->panel->vsc_sdp_supported) ||
 	     msm_dp_wide_bus_available(dp))
